    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is a triangular park with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math> metres. A vertical tower is situated at the mid-point of BC. If the angles of elevation of the top of the tower at, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math> respectively, then the height of the tower (in metres) is",
